    "excerpt": "A burden I would steadfast bear\nAnd watch Your faithful plan supply\nBut easy is my given path\nPerhaps, I scarcely need my guide\n \nChain fetters on me and dismiss\nNeed not be gentle on this boy\nO God, you know me better than this\nYet still I'm lifted on wings of joy.\n\nLet me fight through these weeds\nDig myself out, let me toil\njust give what is coming my way to me\nYet each day I'm planted in new soil\n\nWhy, O Lord,\nWhen justice cuts to bone,\nYou send me not to noose nor sword\nBut invite me to your throne.\n\nRaw Spoon\n",
